  "summary": "The central bank is maintaining its hawkish stance while signaling that price pressures will ease gradually, shaping expectations for monetary policy through next year. Annual price growth eased to 3.12 percent in July, the lowest reading since 2020. Mexico's push to capture manufacturing relocation and AI infrastructure faces a critical constraint: insufficient power generation capacity. The energy deficit directly limits the country's ability to attract the high-consumption industries that are central to its growth strategy.",
